  "sources": [
    {
      "title": "Australia urged to wean off imported fossil fuels amid global supply shocks",
      "link": "https://www.theguardian.com/australia-news/2026/nov/23/australia-urged-to-wean-off-imported-fossil-fuels-amid-global-supply-shocks",
      "description": "<p>Grattan Institute report calls on government to ‘seize’ opportunity to cap diesel tax credits, introduce EV subsidies for less wealthy’ and build ‘clean’ refineries</p><ul><li><p>Get our <a href=\"https://www.theguardian.com/email-newsletters?CMP=cvau_sfl\">daily political email</a>, <a href=\"https://app.adjust.com/w4u7jx3\">free app</a> or <a href=\"https://www.theguardian.com/australia-news/series/full-story?CMP=cvau_sfl\">daily news podcast</a></p></li></ul><p>Capping lucrative diesel tax handouts to big business, building new “clean” refineries and targeting electric vehicle subsidies to less wealthy people could save Australians thousands of dollars in fuel per year, according to a major new report calling on the government to reduce reliance on imported fossil fuels.</p><p>The Grattan Institute, one of the nation’s most respected thinktanks, has warned Australia imports too much of its fuel, and that the country must brace for more global supply shocks – like that from the war in Iran. Under a plan already attracting criticism from business groups, Grattan urged diesel handouts to mining and primary industries be curbed in favour of incentives for electric trucks and a huge expansion of the EV charging network.</p> <a href=\"https://www.theguardian.com/australia-news/2026/nov/23/australia-urged-to-wean-off-imported-fossil-fuels-amid-global-supply-shocks\">Continue reading...</a>",
      "source_name": "The Guardian World",
      "published": "2026-11-22T14:00:29"
    },
    {
      "title": "Police say man whose body lay undiscovered in Sydney bushland for 12 days was killed in suspected hit-and-run",
      "link": "https://www.theguardian.com/australia-news/2026/nov/22/police-say-man-whose-body-lay-undiscovered-in-sydney-bushland-for-12-days-was-killed-in-suspected-hit-and-run-ntwnfb",
      "description": "<p>Joshua Howard, 31, is believed to have been struck by a car and thrown over the guardrail as he was walking home from a party in Rouse Hill</p><ul><li><p>Get our <a href=\"https://www.theguardian.com/email-newsletters?CMP=cvau_sfl\">breaking news email</a>, <a href=\"https://app.adjust.com/w4u7jx3\">free app</a> or <a href=\"https://www.theguardian.com/australia-news/series/full-story?CMP=cvau_sfl\">daily news podcast</a></p></li></ul><p>The twin brother of a man whose body lay undiscovered for 12 days after he was killed in a suspected hit and run in Sydney says it has left him feeling like half a person.</p><p>Joshua Howard was last seen at a bus interchange in Parramatta, in western Sydney, about 10pm on 7 November.</p> <a href=\"https://www.theguardian.com/australia-news/2026/nov/22/police-say-man-whose-body-lay-undiscovered-in-sydney-bushland-for-12-days-was-killed-in-suspected-hit-and-run-ntwnfb\">Continue reading...</a>",
      "source_name": "The Guardian World",
      "published": "2026-11-22T05:21:01"
    }
  ]
